#: views/dahdi_mfcr2_settings.php:229
msgid ""
"You most likely dont need this feature. Default is yes. <br />When this is "
"set to yes, all calls that are offered (incoming calls) for which DNIS is "
"valid (exists in extensions.conf) and also pass collect call validation will "
"be accepted with a Group B tone (either call with charge or not, depending "
"on mfcr2_charge_calls).<br />With this set to 'no' then the call will NOT be "
"accepted on offered and the call will start its execution in extensions.conf "
"without being accepted until the channel is answered (either with Answer() "
"or any other application resulting in the channel being answered). <br /"
">This can be set to 'no' if your telco or PBX needs the hangup cause to be "
"set accurately. <br />When this option is set to 'no' you must explicitly "
"accept the call with DAHDIAcceptR2Call or implicitly through the Answer() "
"application.<br /> <strong>Default:</strong>yes"
msgstr ""
"您很可能不需要此功能。預設為 yes。<br />當此設為 yes 時，所有被提供（來電）且其 DNIS 有效（存在於 extensions.conf 中）並通過對方付費通話驗證的通話，都會以 Group B 音接受（無論是否計費，取決於 mfcr2_charge_calls）。<br />將此設為「no」時，通話不會在提供時被接受，而會開始在 extensions.conf 中執行，直到通道被應答（透過 Answer() 或任何其他會使通道被應答的應用程式）才會被接受。<br />如果您的電信業者或 PBX 需要準確設定掛斷原因，可以將此設為「no」。<br />當此選項設為「no」時，您必須以 DAHDIAcceptR2Call 明確接受通話，或透過 Answer() 應用程式隱含接受。<br /> <strong>預設：</strong>yes"

